:''For the enemy encountered in the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]], see [[The 9th Angel (Enemy)|The 9th Angel]].''
'''The 9th Angel''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event|Evangelion Collaboration Event]]. It was added in [[Version 10.2 Update|Version 10.2]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 551
|rarity = UR
|name1 = The 9th Angel
|name2 = 9th Angel Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''9th Angel Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
The 9th Angel stands to be a nice anti-Alien. While at first glance he seems to have poor DPS, he has a reliable [[Surge Attack|Surge]] that essentially doubles it, though it tends to target the 9th Angel's outward pierce rather than inward pierce. This along with his good [[Long Distance]] coverage and [[Massive Damage]] to Aliens let him pick on any [[Ursamajor]]s and [[LeMurr]]s you come across. He also has the perk of having [[Weaken]]. Its uptime, though with guaranteed procs, is low compared to the 9th Angel's attack rate, however, so it should be considered as a bonus.

Despite having more DPS than [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Aphrodite]], the 9th Angel has flaws when compared to her and snipers in general. He lacks Aphrodite's mobility, survivability, and especially range, which could also mostly be said when comparing him to other snipers such as [[Mami Tomoe (Uber Rare Cat)|Mami Tomoe]]. Having lackluster generalist qualities still doesn't detract from the 9th Angel's Alien nuking capabilities, and thus he remains a good specialist.

{{Job|Classification=Sniper & Nuker}}

